# Documentation ships markdown, Word, and PDF (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-09-27), verbatim:

> **Generate DOCX and PDFs when you generate .MD files. Make sure that the
> MD, PDFs and DOCX are pushed to the docs repo consistently. You can
> create additional subdirectories in the docs repo that will be part of
> the repo. Do not .gitignore documentation. Make sure that all canvases
> are also implemented as DOCX and PDF. Timestamp all PDF and DOCX in
> headers and use page numbering.**

## The rule

> **A documentation markdown file is delivered when its Word (`.docx`) and
> Portable Document Format (`.pdf`) twins exist beside it and all three are
> committed and pushed together. Every rendered header carries the provider
> name, the document title, and the generation timestamp. Every rendered
> footer carries Page X of Y. Canvases ship the same two renders.
> Documentation is never added to `.gitignore`.**

## 1. The renderer

Use `operator-workflows/scripts/docs/render-doc.py`. Do not write a second
renderer, and do not hand-build Word files.

```powershell
# One or more files
python c:\analog-pim\operator-workflows\scripts\docs\render-doc.py path\to\doc.md

# A whole directory
python ...\render-doc.py --dir c:\analog-pim\pam-platform-docs\docs\go-to-market --glob "*.md"

# Word only, when Word COM is unavailable
python ...\render-doc.py path\to\doc.md --docx-only

# Parser self-test
python ...\render-doc.py --self-test
```

It writes United States Letter pages with one-inch margins, renders
headings, tables, lists, block quotes, code blocks, and inline emphasis,
then exports the PDF through Microsoft Word so the page-count field
resolves. A batch shares one Word session, so rendering a directory does
not pay Word startup per file.

**Host toolchain, measured 2026-09-27 - do not re-probe this every
session** ([`ascii-syntax-and-powershell-first-run.mdc`](ascii-syntax-and-powershell-first-run.mdc)
section 5):

| Tool | State | Consequence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `python-docx` | Present (1.2.0) | Word output works |
| `pywin32` and Microsoft Word | Present (Word 16.0) | PDF export works through COM |
| `pdfplumber`, `pypdf` | Present | Use them to read a rendered PDF back and verify header, timestamp, and page count |
| `pandoc` | **Absent** | Do not write a pipeline that assumes it |
| LibreOffice / `soffice` | **Absent** | No headless-conversion fallback |
| `reportlab`, `weasyprint` | **Absent** | There is no direct PDF writer; Word COM is the only PDF path |

Legal instruments are **not** covered here. Contracts keep
`operator-workflows/scripts/contracts/render-contract.py` and the header,
revision-date, and render rules in
[`gtm-contracts-render-commit-push.mdc`](gtm-contracts-render-commit-push.mdc)
and [`gtm-price-list-revision-date.mdc`](gtm-price-list-revision-date.mdc).

## 2. House style, cover page, header and footer

Every rendered document uses the AIC house style described in
`pam-platform-docs/docs/DOCUMENT-STYLE.md`: a cover page (navy band with
the unmodified `core-assets/branding/aic-logo-white.png`, the company name
in Arial, the title in large navy Arial, title case), Arial 12 point
body, navy title-case headings, and navy-header zebra tables. Arial is
the default for corporate communication and manuals. If Arial is not
installed, use the closest Helvetica equivalent that is installed, and
ask for Helvetica when none of those faces is present. Do not use
Calibri. The cover
page is mandatory; there is no opt-out. The `<!-- briefing -->` mark only
moves the subtitle and byline lines onto the cover. Never add a name or
email address to a document that did not already carry one.

| Position | Content |
| --- | --- |
| Cover page | No running header. Footer is the copyright line, then the page number. The cover also prints the copyright statement under the rule |
| Header line 1 | `Analog Informatics Corporation - <document title>`, taken from the first level-one heading |
| Header line 2 | `Generated YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM UTC` |
| Footer | `Copyright © <year> Analog Informatics Corporation. All rights reserved.` then `Page X of Y`, centered. Page numbers are Word `PAGE` and `NUMPAGES` fields |

The timestamp records when the file was rendered. It is a record of an
event, not a prediction, so it does not conflict with the ban on duration
estimates in
[`us-terminology-word-choice.mdc`](us-terminology-word-choice.mdc).

Page numbering must come from Word fields. A hardcoded page number is
wrong the moment pagination changes.

## 3. Canvases

A canvas (`*.canvas.tsx`) is source for an interactive view and cannot be
rendered directly. Each canvas therefore has a **markdown twin** in the
repo, which is already the convention for rate-card canvases, and that
twin renders to Word and PDF like any other document. A canvas with no
markdown twin is incomplete: author the twin, then render it.

## 4. Never gitignore documentation

Documentation and its renders are repository content. Do not add
markdown, Word, or PDF paths to `.gitignore`, and remove any existing
entry that excludes documentation. Binary renders are committed even
though they are binaries.

New subdirectories are allowed and expected. Create them under the docs
tree and index them in the nearest `README.md`.

**Open item, not an approval:** `pam-platform-docs/.gitignore` currently
excludes `docs/go-to-market/contracts/generated/*`, which holds `-filled`
contract render output whose counterpart copies are tracked in the family
folders. That entry predates this rule and is under review. Do not cite it
as precedent for ignoring anything else.

## 5. Commit together

Markdown, Word, and PDF land in the **same commit**. A commit carrying
only the markdown leaves the repository inconsistent, which is the specific
failure this rule prevents. Stage by explicit path
([`shared-working-tree-is-not-yours.mdc`](shared-working-tree-is-not-yours.mdc)),
then push ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

When markdown changes later, re-render both twins in that change set. A
stale Word or PDF beside updated markdown is a defect.

## Forbidden constructs

- Committing documentation markdown without its Word and PDF twins.
- A Word or PDF whose content is older than the markdown beside it.
- Adding any documentation path to `.gitignore`.
- A rendered file with no timestamp in the header, or with no page
  numbering in the footer.
- A hardcoded page number or page count.
- A canvas with no markdown twin, or a twin that is never rendered.
- A second markdown-to-Word renderer, or hand-assembled Word output.
- Rendering contracts with this script instead of the contracts renderer.

## Required agent behavior

1. After writing or editing any documentation markdown, run the renderer
   on it before committing.
2. Stage the `.md`, `.docx`, and `.pdf` together by explicit path.
3. State in the report which files were rendered.
4. If Word COM is unavailable, render with `--docx-only`, say that the PDF
   is missing and why, and do not describe the document set as complete.
5. Mirror this file to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change set.
   The workspace `.cursor` directory is not a git root.

